{"title":"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">2004 AMC 12B #10</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10B Problems\">2004 AMC 10B #12</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An annulus is the region between two concentric circles. The concentric circles in the figure have radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd3932fd8be042b3b42f1e4bd56fbd1902b1c3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a903f7c677cbaadb6e72741b95730648ab1d442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> be a radius of the larger circle, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb2419be49ff83cbed7db9a2f366858ccabf2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XZ$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> be tangent to the smaller circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afe773cd5709ee6b1f9f84680829802825cfab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OY$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> be the radius of the larger circle that contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866d92a48eb831ff5c70b73e13313adfdbeb7ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=XZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8ba9c97c3ba09034c27152dc55f71b0534b17e36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=YZ$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7ae3f367a4080971e73933e8903ddd7e2ea5aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e=XY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of the annulus? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0ca2ea60f3f8c72bd6e0bb1dd3335aaf69a85ba9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1.5cm); defaultpen(0.8); real r1=1.5, r2=2.5; pair O=(0,0); path inner=Circle(O,r1), outer=Circle(O,r2); pair Y=(0,r2), Z=(0,r1), X=intersectionpoint( Z--(Z+(10,0)), outer ); filldraw(outer,lightgray,black); filldraw(inner,white,black); draw(X--O--Y); draw(Y--X--Z); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,SW); label(&quot;$X$&quot;,X,E); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,Y,N); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;,Z,SW); label(&quot;$a$&quot;,X--Z,N); label(&quot;$b$&quot;,0.25*X,SE); label(&quot;$c$&quot;,O--Z,E); label(&quot;$d$&quot;,Y--Z,W); label(&quot;$e$&quot;,Y*0.65 + X*0.35,SW); defaultpen(0.5); dot(O); dot(X); dot(Z); dot(Y); [/asy]\" width=\"358\" height=\"378\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cdec9c388f68af76ed27a201f7be85c80df158ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\pi a^2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\pi b^2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\pi c^2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\pi d^2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\pi e^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"431\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the large circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07ff2e57aac6f778fd2b55ef4a84e2146100ce21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi b^2$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, the area of the small one is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d5886c620e20256c8c7affa32f8553c878a02330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi c^2$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, hence the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11eb915d77533ba2fa67e0387ecfc80d81f4def.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(b^2-c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>From the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> for the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/985ae45cc9db06e55d850b8f8c045fd834ad202a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OXZ$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969a16c3e4948fe6fb474d0a1b5bd5758b5d8fc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + c^2 = b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4acf77bc9317800efa3fe0859fdbf21bd0a368c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2-c^2=a^2$\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> and thus the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c356cd9aefe57dc7c0a323ce7ac58733b2cac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)\\ }\\pi a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/3019fd0bdd49207edd86f39a69fcdc0ab6d9a367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> then the shaded area is just the area of a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8acfd7d5ee559262593701b8dbd02e43ad96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c356cd9aefe57dc7c0a323ce7ac58733b2cac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)\\ }\\pi a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"73\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B\">2004 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12B_Problems/Probl